Well, you could dip them in holy water. To get holy water, you need
potions of water ("clear potion") a coaligned altar, and it being safe
to pray. if you drop the waters on the altar and pray over them, your
god will bless them (if he isn't angry at you or the prayer timer isn't
out) and they'll become holy water. Of course, if you try this on
another god's altar, they'll become holy water (cursing dipped items),
and your god will become angry, and your alignment will suffer.

If you go into a shop and a water ("clear potion", if not yet ID'd)
costs about 150 zormikands, that's probably holy water.

Spellbooks/scrolls won't be erased by holy water, and nothing will
suffer the effects of being wet.

If you're talking about a weapon, you could just wield it and pray to
your god--kind of risky, but if nothing else is wrong, and it's safe to
pray, your god could uncurse it. Doesn't work with armor or
accessories, though.

Not really removing the curse, but if you accidently put on a cursed
armor or accessory, you can drop everything else and try to get a nymph
to steal it, or a succubus to take it off.

Also, if you're dying so much, why not try an easier class, like
Barbarian or Valkyrie, for a little while? I just got back into
Nethack, and was leaving so many Wizard bone files I could barely play
for fleeing ghosts--then I discovered how much newbie-frendlier it was
to play as a Valkyrie.

